            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rob DeWayne Strickland"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It was delicious. But I used 1 TBLS. Of zest an 1/3 cup of lemon juice an 3/4 cup of water give a little more lemon zing. Thanks for the recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2020-07-05T20:11:07.677Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Shayla"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I halved the sugar and doubled the lemon juice. With a dollop of Cool Whip on top, that sweetness level works for me. Some may disagree. If I were making it for a potluck or something, I might add 1/8-1/4 cup more sugar, because I feel like most people would like it just a little sweeter. \nI'm not much of a baker or a cook, so I've never dealt with lemon zest before. The one lemon I bought only made less than half a teaspoon and it called for a whole teaspoon. I will probably just leave the zest out next time because I don't think it makes much difference.",
            "datePublished": "2021-07-24T09:35:08.350Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "flutterby812"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this last night and it's delicious!! Very nice natural lemon flavor. (Not jello or pudding!) . I also like the process making the custard instead of the recipes I've seen using sweetened condensed milk and cool whip. The end result is definitely worth those extra few minutes! I made this pie with a Biscoff Cookie crust. YUM!! 10/10 would recommend!!!",
            "datePublished": "2026-09-12T18:30:52.431Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Joy Kahler"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This worked out really well! People said it didn’t have enough flavor, but I didn’t measure my lemon juice so I’m not sure what the regular recipe is like. I used the juice of a good sized lemon and it was packed with flavor! I also did a graham cracker crust and added some candies lemon peel on top for texture",
            "datePublished": "2019-06-02T16:14:24.297Z"
          },
